\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {FALI constructs a 32-cell counterfactual intervention game for the selected attention head.} (a) Structurally valid pre-softmax scores are partitioned into the prespecified task-target coordinate(s) $T$, rival scores $R$ in the same task-relevant query row, and all other valid scores $O$; masked coordinates are not players. (b) Each hybrid cell selects $T,R,O,V,$ and $C$ from the intact or perturbed endpoint, reconstructs the candidate attention pattern and head output, and defines utility relative to a candidate-zero run in the same surrounding context $C$. (c) All $2^5=32$ hybrid states are evaluated. Standard Owen attribution under $\mathrm  {SCORE}=\{T,R,O\}$, $\mathrm  {VALUE}=\{V\}$, and $\mathrm  {CONTEXT}=\{C\}$ allocates the endpoint change over 36 block-contiguous admissible permutations, satisfying $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _i\phi _i=\Delta _h$ and $\Phi _{\mathrm  {SCORE}}=\phi _T+\phi _R+\phi _O$. The mixed cells are controlled counterfactual states, not claims that the model naturally implements five independent causal pathways.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fali-game}{{2}{11}{\textbf {FALI constructs a 32-cell counterfactual intervention game for the selected attention head.} (a) Structurally valid pre-softmax scores are partitioned into the prespecified task-target coordinate(s) $T$, rival scores $R$ in the same task-relevant query row, and all other valid scores $O$; masked coordinates are not players. (b) Each hybrid cell selects $T,R,O,V,$ and $C$ from the intact or perturbed endpoint, reconstructs the candidate attention pattern and head output, and defines utility relative to a candidate-zero run in the same surrounding context $C$. (c) All $2^5=32$ hybrid states are evaluated. Standard Owen attribution under $\mathrm {SCORE}=\{T,R,O\}$, $\mathrm {VALUE}=\{V\}$, and $\mathrm {CONTEXT}=\{C\}$ allocates the endpoint change over 36 block-contiguous admissible permutations, satisfying $\sum _i\phi _i=\Delta _h$ and $\Phi _{\mathrm {SCORE}}=\phi _T+\phi _R+\phi _O$. The mixed cells are controlled counterfactual states, not claims that the model naturally implements five independent causal pathways}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{eq:owen-value}{{17}{11}{Standard Owen attribution and coarse--fine reconciliation}{equation.17}{}}
\newlabel{eq:owen-efficiency}{{18}{12}{Standard Owen attribution and coarse--fine reconciliation}{equation.18}{}}
\newlabel{eq:quotient-game}{{19}{12}{Standard Owen attribution and coarse--fine reconciliation}{equation.19}{}}
\newlabel{eq:quotient-consistency}{{22}{12}{Standard Owen attribution and coarse--fine reconciliation}{equation.22}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {5}Method Validation}{12}{section.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:validation}{{5}{12}{Method Validation}{section.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Controlled validation recovers known factors, interaction allocation, and transformer endpoint identities.} (a) In five deterministic single-factor systems, the manipulated factor receives the full endpoint change: each row shows the recovery ratio $\phi _j/\Delta U_i$, with the raw injected $\Delta U_i$ given beside the row. The maximum attribution discrepancy is $1.11\times 10^{-16}$. (b) A pure $T\times C$ construction with $\Delta U\approx 2$ yields the analytically expected Owen split $\phi _T\approx 1$ and $\phi _C\approx 1$, with $R,O,V=0$. (c) In the randomly initialized two-layer TransformerLens validation model, independently measured intact effect, conditional effect, and conditional gain are $0.455046$, $-0.085684$, and $-0.540729$, respectively, and the corresponding FALI endpoint cells reproduce them exactly at recorded precision. Reconstruction, leakage, and model-level quotient residuals are zero at recorded precision. These are implementation and controlled-ground-truth checks, not evidence that mixed FALI hybrids are unique natural model pathways.}}{13}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:validation}{{3}{13}{\textbf {Controlled validation recovers known factors, interaction allocation, and transformer endpoint identities.} (a) In five deterministic single-factor systems, the manipulated factor receives the full endpoint change: each row shows the recovery ratio $\phi _j/\Delta U_i$, with the raw injected $\Delta U_i$ given beside the row. The maximum attribution discrepancy is $1.11\times 10^{-16}$. (b) A pure $T\times C$ construction with $\Delta U\approx 2$ yields the analytically expected Owen split $\phi _T\approx 1$ and $\phi _C\approx 1$, with $R,O,V=0$. (c) In the randomly initialized two-layer TransformerLens validation model, independently measured intact effect, conditional effect, and conditional gain are $0.455046$, $-0.085684$, and $-0.540729$, respectively, and the corresponding FALI endpoint cells reproduce them exactly at recorded precision. Reconstruction, leakage, and model-level quotient residuals are zero at recorded precision. These are implementation and controlled-ground-truth checks, not evidence that mixed FALI hybrids are unique natural model pathways}{figure.3}{}}
